    "prompt": "A DevOps engineer updates an A record in Route 53 from IP 1.2.3.4 to 5.6.7.8 with a TTL of 300 seconds. Some external users still reach 1.2.3.4 for up to an hour. Why?",
    "explanation": "While the Authoritative nameserver (Route 53) updates immediately, intermediate Recursive DNS resolvers (like ISP resolvers or corporate forwarders) cache DNS responses for the duration of the TTL. Some misconfigured recursive resolvers also enforce minimum cache times, or client browser DNS caches ignore short TTLs.",
    "hintsJson": "[\"Recursive resolvers and local browser caches hold onto responses until cache expiry.\"]",
